nd()`, `.pop()`, slicing, and support for dictionaries would improve its capabilities. This could bridge the feature gap between the local JavaScript interpreter and the more robust Python execution environment, improving its utility in offline scenarios \n<truncated 9192 bytes>\nic event types like \"LOOP_ITER\", \"LOOP_END\", \"CONDITION\", \"AUG_ASSIGN\", \"ASSIGN\", and \"PRINT\" to the `eventType` field based on `ast` node types. Included detailed operation details in `operationDetail` to provide rich execution data. Also planned to review sub-expression frame generation.\n\n\nExamining the Python engine's sub-expression frame generation logic, aiming for complete and consistent data capture during code tracing. The goal is to accurately trace the evaluation of complex expressions. The evaluation of sub-expression frames will be checked, starting with `ast.BoolOp` nodes, to capture frames in the case of short-circuiting.\n\nThe planned post-order traversal of sub-expressions is expected to provide correct evaluation order. At each step, a new frame will be created. The expression will be formatted. The replacement will track expression evaluation at all levels of complexity (e.g., AST node type).\n\n\nEnhanced variable alignment logic to capture variable values after the final line execution in top-level scripts. Implemented a test to verify correct capture of final variable states when no explicit `return` exists. Updated the `engine.py` logic to track final values.\n\nInvestigated short-circuiting behavior within `ast.BoolOp` nodes. Initiated post-order traversal of sub-expressions to create frames at each step during code execution. Formatting of expressions and tracking of evaluation is in progress.\n\n\nDuplicate files in the root directory were identified and marked for removal to streamline the project structure, with only the updated versions within `app_build/` to be preserved after validating all dependencies.  Planned cleaning of unused code within several `app_build/` files was also outlined to improve code efficiency. The Python engine's trace data format will be revised to precisely mirror the UI's expected format, particularly by updating the `eventType` field with more detailed values corresponding to distinct events during code execution. The current focus is on a review and code cleanup.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\napp_build/engine.py — Universal Beginner & DSA Python Execution Tracer\\nZero AI APIs. Uses Python's native `ast` module and `sys.settrace` in a safe sandbox.\\nSupports:\\n- Any standalone function (`def binary_search(arr, target):`, `def two_sum(nums, target):`, etc.)\\n- Any LeetCode-style `class Solution:` method (`maxSubArray`, `twoSum`, `search`, etc.)\\n- Top-level scripts, recursion, loops, dicts, sets, lists, strings, slicing, comprehensions\\n- Thonny-style AST Sub-Expression Stepper with Short-Circuit ('and' / 'or') evaluation\\n- Stack & Heap Reference Model (Name -> @Address -> Value) with Visual Garbage Collection\\n- Global vs. Local Scope Isolation across the call stack\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport ast\\nimport builtins\\nimport copy\\nimport io\\nimport sys\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\nSUPPORTED_BUILTINS = {\\n    \\\"__build_class__\\\": builtins.__build_class__,\\n    \\\"__name__\\\": \\\"__main__\\\",\\n    \\\"object\\\": object,\\n    \\\"abs\\\": abs,\\n    \\\"all\\\": all,\\n    \\\"any\\\": any,\\n    \\\"bool\\\": bool,\\n    \\\"chr\\\": chr,\\n    \\\"dict\\\": dict,\\n    \\\"divmod\\\": divmod,\\n    \\\"enumerate\\\": enumerate,\\n    \\\"filter\\\": filter,\\n    \\\"float\\\": float,\\n    \\\"hex\\\": hex,\\n    \\\"int\\\": int,\\n    \\\"isinstance\\\": isinstance,\\n    \\\"len\\\": len,\\n    \\\"list\\\": list,\\n    \\\"map\\\": map,\\n    \\\"max\\\": max,\\n    \\\"min\\\": min,\\n    \\\"ord\\\": ord,\\n    \\\"pow\\\": pow,\\n    \\\"print\\\": print,\\n    \\\"range\\\": range,\\n    \\\"reversed\\\": reversed,\\n    \\\"round\\\": round,\\n    \\\"set\\\": set,\\n    \\\"sorted\\\": sorted,\\n    \\\"str\\\": str,\\n    \\\"sum\\\": sum,\\n    \\\"tuple\\\": tuple,\\n    \\\"type\\\": type,\\n    \\\"zip\\\": zip,\\n    # Common typing annotations used in DSA / LeetCode snippets\\n    \\\"List\\\": list,\\n    \\\"Dict\\\": dict,\\n    \\\"Set\\\": set,\\n    \\\"Tuple\\\": tuple,\\n    \\\"Optional\\\": object,\\n    \\\"Any\\\": object,\\n    \\\"True\\\": True,\\n    \\\"False\\\": False,\\n    \\\"None\\\": None,\\n    \\\"Exception\\\": Exception,\\n    \\\"IndexError\\\": IndexError,\\n    \\\"ValueError\\\": ValueError,\\n    \\\"TypeError\\\": TypeError,\\n    \\\"KeyError\\\": KeyEr\n<truncated 41072 bytes>","Description":"\"Upgrade app_build/engine.py to support any Python/DSA code with universal parameter synthesis, post-order AST sub-expression reduction, and full eventType alignment\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\code-flow-visualizer\\\\app_build\\\\engine.py\"","toolAction":"\"Upgrading app_build/engine.py for universal DSA support\"","toolSummary":"\"Upgrade app_build/engine.py for universal DSA support\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
